V(mu + sigma/sqrt2) = 1/4*sqrt(2)*lam*mu*sig^3 + 1/2*lam*mu^2*sig^2 + 1/16*lam*sig^4
Higgs mass^2 (twice the sigma^2 coefficient): lam*mu^2
gauge boson mass^2 m_A^2 = 2 e^2 mu^2 -> 2*e^2*mu^2
degrees of freedom: before (2 real scalars + 2 photon polarisations) = 4 ; after (1 Higgs + 3 massive-vector polarisations) = 4
